#document(
  default_font = "Helvetica",
  default_size = pt(11),
  page = { size = "letter", orientation = "portrait" },
  margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) }
)
#style(
  name = "Normal",
  type = "paragraph",
  run = { font = "Helvetica", size = pt(11) },
  paragraph = { spacing = { before = pt(0), after = pt(0), line = { rule = "exact", value = pt(20) } } }
)

LINE BASELINE: Word sets the baseline of an automatic line below the line gap and ascender of its font, and places the space a multiple adds beneath the descender. Each sample lies between exact reference lines, whose baselines are known.

#style(
  name = "S1",
  type = "paragraph",
  based_on = "Normal",
  run = { font = "Helvetica", size = pt(11) },
  paragraph = { spacing = { before = pt(0), after = pt(0), line = { rule = "multiple", value = 0.8 } } }
)

Reference 001.

#paragraph(style = "S1")[Helvetica 11 multiple 0.8 first.]

#paragraph(style = "S1")[Helvetica 11 multiple 0.8 second.]

